      "text": "The name Africa in miniature extends  to more than just the Geography actually. \nMost countries in Africa either speak French or English as they were colonized at some point by France or England. Cameroon happens to be the only country in Africa that was simultaneously a colony of both Britain and France after WW2. \nThis means French and English are both Official languages and we have English Speaking natives to the west bordering Nigeria and French Speaking natives to the East and South bordering other Central African countries...\nIt's either French or English everywhere else. Cameroon has both",
